From fdad4da2291bd37eb176470457a60be4a8807d30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:50:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_remote_notices: each silent sweep skip and
 live-poller claim logs once per reason; pin the busy non-owner hand-back for
 remote notices

t_01a1d46be379dfd3. t_01a1d405586c5ba1's done notice reached chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6 95 min after it
completed although the Mac observed it in 63 s: a busy Desktop backend's legacy poller held the remote claim
in flight until its own turn ended, and the owner's sweep skipped it with no log line, so the delay was filed
as 46 min of discovery lag.

- _deliver_link names why it skips an undelivered notice (claim in flight under backend pid N, chat open in
  this backend, left to the gateway's FIFO), once per (chat, ref, state, reason); collect logs which backend's
  live poller claimed it, once per reason.
- Regression test: a busy non-owner backend hands a REMOTE claim back on its next poll once the gateway owns
  the chat (06e164b139's hand-back; RED with that branch disabled, i.e. the 2cc7101849 behaviour).
